    "updated_at": "2016-04-05T15:40:03Z",
    "body": "@inikulin Yeah, I saw how parse5 implemented it, but this extra state is a bit redundant IMO. In linked commit it works without this extra state, although implementation will be surely still free to perform own optimizations specific to its needs (they don't necessarily even need to implement actual state machine after all :) ), and as for the spec itself I'd prefer it to be as minimal and clean as possible.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
